{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Time and Observers","modules":[{"name":"AstronomyKit"}],"role":"article"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/TimeAndObservers"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/astronomykit\/timeandobservers"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Work with astronomical time and geographic observer locations."}],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit"]]},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/GettingStarted"],"generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Accurate time handling is fundamental to astronomy. AstronomyKit provides "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstroTime","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for precise time representation and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Observer","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for geographic locations."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Working with Time","anchor":"Working-with-Time","type":"heading"},{"level":3,"text":"Creating Times","anchor":"Creating-Times","type":"heading"},{"code":["\/\/ Current time","let now = AstroTime.now","","\/\/ From calendar components (in UTC)","let eclipse = AstroTime(year: 2024, month: 4, day: 8, hour: 18, minute: 15)","","\/\/ From Foundation Date","let time = AstroTime(Date())","","\/\/ From Julian days since J2000","let jd = AstroTime(ut: 9132.5)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"Time Arithmetic","anchor":"Time-Arithmetic","type":"heading"},{"code":["let now = AstroTime.now","","\/\/ Add days or hours","let tomorrow = now.addingDays(1)","let nextHour = now.addingHours(1)","let lastWeek = now.addingDays(-7)","","\/\/ Compare times","if tomorrow > now {","    print(\"Tomorrow comes after now\")","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"Converting to Date","anchor":"Converting-to-Date","type":"heading"},{"code":["let time = AstroTime.now","let date: Date = time.date","","\/\/ Format for display","let formatter = DateFormatter()","formatter.dateStyle = .medium","formatter.timeStyle = .short","print(formatter.string(from: time.date))"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"Understanding UT vs TT","anchor":"Understanding-UT-vs-TT","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"AstroTime stores two time values internally:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Universal Time (UT)"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Based on Earth’s rotation, used for rise\/set times","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Terrestrial Time (TT)"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Uniform time scale, used for planetary orbits"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"code":["let time = AstroTime.now","print(\"UT: \\(time.universalTime)\")  \/\/ Days since J2000 noon (UTC)","print(\"TT: \\(time.terrestrialTime)\")  \/\/ Days since J2000 noon (TT)","","\/\/ Create from Terrestrial Time directly","let fromTT = AstroTime(tt: 9132.5)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The difference (ΔT) is automatically handled by AstronomyKit.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Accepted Range","level":3,"anchor":"Accepted-Range"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Positions, states, distances, and the searches built on them accept a Terrestrial Time within 4,000 Julian years of J2000: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"abs(time.terrestrialTime) <= 1_461_000"},{"text":" days, roughly the years −2000 to +6000. That is about the span over which the VSOP87 planetary theory claims validity. Outside it, and for a non-finite time, they throw ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstronomyError\/badTime"},{"text":". Pluto accepts a narrower span, about the years −100 to +4100.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A calculation that samples nearby times can throw within a short distance of either edge: light-travel correction looks back up to a few hours, the Moon’s state vectors sample about a second either side, and searches step by days to years, sometimes backward before stepping forward. Creating an ","type":"text"},{"code":"AstroTime","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" outside the range is not an error; only the calculations reject it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Delta T Configuration","level":3,"anchor":"Delta-T-Configuration"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The difference between TT and UT (called ΔT) varies over time and is estimated using a model. AstronomyKit defaults to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/DeltaTModel\/observed"},{"text":", a yearly table of IERS Earth-rotation values that is extrapolated beyond its last entry. You can switch to Espenak-Meeus or, for compatibility, JPL Horizons:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["\/\/ Switch to JPL Horizons Delta T model","AstronomyConfig.setDeltaTModel(.jplHorizons)","","\/\/ Query Delta T for a specific time","let deltaT = AstronomyConfig.deltaTObserved(universalTime: 0)  \/\/ Seconds at J2000","","\/\/ Restore the default","AstronomyConfig.setDeltaTModel(.observed)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","text":"Sidereal Time","level":3,"anchor":"Sidereal-Time"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Get the sidereal time at the prime meridian:"}]},{"code":["let sidereal = AstroTime.now.siderealTime","print(\"Greenwich Sidereal Time: \\(sidereal) hours\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Calculate local sidereal time for any longitude:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let observer = Observer(latitude: 40.7, longitude: -74.0)  \/\/ NYC","let lst = AstroTime.now.siderealTime(longitude: observer.longitude)","print(\"Local Sidereal Time: \\(lst) hours\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The result is in 0 up to, but not including, 24 hours for any finite longitude. An infinite or NaN longitude returns ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".nan"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Working-with-Observers","text":"Working with Observers","type":"heading","level":2},{"anchor":"Creating-Observers","text":"Creating Observers","type":"heading","level":3},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Basic location (sea level)","let seattle = Observer(latitude: 47.6062, longitude: -122.3321)","","\/\/ With height above sea level (meters)","let everest = Observer(","    latitude: 27.9881,","    longitude: 86.9250,","    height: 8848.86",")"]},{"anchor":"Coordinate-Conventions","text":"Coordinate Conventions","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Latitude","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": -90° (south) to +90° (north)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Longitude"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": -180° (west) to +180° (east)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Height","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": Meters above sea level"}]}]}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Built-in-Locations","text":"Built-in Locations","type":"heading"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let greenwich = Observer.greenwich       \/\/ Royal Observatory","let primeMeridian = Observer.primeMeridian  \/\/ 0°, 0°"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Observer-Properties","level":3,"text":"Observer Properties"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let observer = Observer(latitude: 40.0, longitude: -105.0, height: 1600)","","\/\/ Local gravity (accounts for latitude and altitude)","let gravity = observer.gravity  \/\/ m\/s²","","\/\/ Atmospheric conditions at this elevation","let atmosphere = try observer.atmosphere","print(\"Pressure: \\(atmosphere.pressure) mbar\")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Observer-Vectors","level":3,"text":"Observer Vectors"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Get the observer’s position relative to Earth’s center:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let observer = Observer.greenwich","","\/\/ Position vector in AU","let position = try observer.vector(at: .now)","","\/\/ Full state (position and velocity)","let state = try observer.state(at: .now)","print(\"Position: \\(state.position)\")","print(\"Velocity: \\(state.velocity)\")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Time-Zones","level":2,"text":"Time Zones"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"AstronomyKit works entirely in UTC. Convert to local time using Foundation:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let sunrise = try CelestialBody.sun.riseTime(after: .now, from: observer)!","","let formatter = DateFormatter()","formatter.timeZone = TimeZone(identifier: \"America\/New_York\")","formatter.timeStyle = .short","print(\"Sunrise (local): \\(formatter.string(from: sunrise.date))\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"text":"Codable Support","anchor":"Codable-Support","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Both types support ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for persistence:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let observer = Observer(latitude: 40.7, longitude: -74.0)","let data = try JSONEncoder().encode(observer)","","let time = AstroTime.now","let timeData = try JSONEncoder().encode(time)"],"syntax":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://AstronomyKit/documentation/AstronomyKit/Observer":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Observer","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Observer","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Observer","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A geographic location for observing celestial objects."}],"title":"Observer","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/astronomykit\/observer"},"doc://AstronomyKit/documentation/AstronomyKit":{"title":"AstronomyKit","role":"collection","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit","url":"\/documentation\/astronomykit","abstract":[{"text":"Swift bindings for Don Cross’ ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/cosinekitty\/astronomy","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" library.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://AstronomyKit/documentation/AstronomyKit/AstroTime":{"kind":"symbol","title":"AstroTime","url":"\/documentation\/astronomykit\/astrotime","abstract":[{"text":"Represents a moment in time for astronomical calculations.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstroTime","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AstroTime"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AstroTime","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://AstronomyKit/documentation/AstronomyKit/DeltaTModel/observed":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/DeltaTModel\/observed","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"observed","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"DeltaTModel.observed","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Observed Earth rotation (default).","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/astronomykit\/deltatmodel\/observed"},"doc://AstronomyKit/documentation/AstronomyKit/GettingStarted":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/GettingStarted","type":"topic","title":"Getting Started with AstronomyKit","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/astronomykit\/gettingstarted","abstract":[{"text":"Learn how to add AstronomyKit to your project and perform basic astronomical calculations.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"https://github.com/cosinekitty/astronomy":{"title":"Astronomy Engine","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/cosinekitty\/astronomy","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/cosinekitty\/astronomy","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Astronomy Engine","type":"text"}],"type":"link"},"doc://AstronomyKit/documentation/AstronomyKit/AstronomyError/badTime":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"AstronomyError.badTime","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The provided date\/time is outside the allowed range."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"badTime","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstronomyError\/badTime","url":"\/documentation\/astronomykit\/astronomyerror\/badtime"}}}